    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d890">

                <pb facs="1032" n="914" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg914"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">662.11173 Barley/38: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Poole</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase—Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-24T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                                1928—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 24—10:05
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>217.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Reference my 215, October 23, 10 a.m. According to very confidential information,
                    yesterday at stormy meeting private interests <pb facs="1033" n="915"
                        xml:id="pg915"/> and competent ministries decided for present to defer
                    embargo. Its proponents were embarrassed because of failure of scientific
                    investigation so far to produce definite explanation regarding barley’s alleged
                    nocuous character.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Poole</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
